invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64.h
catches: rsa_equiv_test_compare
reason: the compare form of rsa_mont64_mul_add_add, which clang reads,
  drops the carry of its second add, the carry in from the word below,
  so the step's high word is one short whenever that add wraps, which a
  random word does about half the time. bin/rsa_equiv_test_compare runs
  that form under any compiler and compares the bytes with the 32-bit
  arm's.

--- old
    high += (uint64_t)(second < first);
--- new
    (void)first;
